From c69353956b22c9d7d6a732cc9a1845a1ebced58b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 06:39:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/63] Offer the main settings on the welcome screen

The first launch now asks about the handful of things people change first:
search engine, address bar position, autofill provider, an external download
manager, the ad blocker, and background media. Everything keeps the defaults it
has elsewhere, so tapping straight through changes nothing.

Rows that are simply on or off use a switch. Rows with several answers open a
chooser written to match the screen it opens from, rather than the platform
list dialog, which looked borrowed. The download manager row lists the apps
actually installed, since turning the setting on without saying where downloads
should go would just make Android ask every time.

The screen follows the device's light and dark setting instead of always being
black.

Two things this fixes. The welcome is now only spent once Start is pressed:
leaving before that used to count as having seen it, so the browser came back
with defaults nobody chose and no way to reach the screen again. And the ad
blocker switch is read by the bundled extension loader, which is why its key
lives in shared preferences rather than profile prefs: the loader runs in C++
before profile prefs exist.
